# Git rules

- Author identity is set repo-locally: `Devu Dilip <devu.dilip@gmail.com>`. Never change it.
- **Commit after every working unit** — a component that renders, a script that runs, a doc that is complete. Small commits, many of them. Never leave a session with uncommitted work that typechecks.
- Before committing: `npm run typecheck` must pass. Do not commit `node_modules`, `.next`, or `data/raw`.

## Message format (Conventional Commits)

```
<type>(<scope>): <imperative summary under 72 chars>

optional body explaining why, not what
```

Types: `feat`, `fix`, `data` (corpus/dictionary content), `style` (visual only), `docs`, `chore`, `refactor`, `test`.
Scopes: `dict`, `reader`, `ui`, `pwa`, `brand`, `scripts`, `rules`, `corpus`.

Examples:

```
feat(reader): add measurement-based pagination engine
data(corpus): add Sarvajna tripadi selection with provenance
style(ui): tighten bottom nav spacing on small screens
```

- Contributors sign off with DCO (`git commit -s`) and retain their own copyright. No CLA, no copyright assignment — ever.
